1
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:12,680
Go!
Comrades. Go!

2
00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:22,080
Nothing.
There's nothing too.

3
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:29,240
Ahh!

4
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:33,320
It's a trap!

5
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:34,720
Take cover!

6
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:49,960
Comrade Fah, take everyone to
the edge of the forest.

7
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:51,280
Ouch!
Hurry!

8
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:54,639
I'll provide cover while you move.

9
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:55,800
Get back, Comrade.

10
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:01,080
Hey! Comrade.

11
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:03,479
Comrade! Damn!

12
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:04,759
Argh!

13
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:08,560
Comrade Fah, hurry up!

14
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:10,200
Go.

15
00:01:10,201 --> 00:01:11,840
Argh!

16
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:14,519
Argh!

17
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:16,400
Comrade Fah, how's it going?

18
00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:18,480
I'm OK.

19
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:21,960
Take our comrades safely back to the base.

20
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:24,240
No, I'll go with Comrade Ploeng.

21
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:26,440
Go!

22
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:29,880
Stick to our ideology,

23
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:32,080
Go!

24
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:37,120
Get back, Comrade.

25
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:39,280
Ouch!

26
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:57,400
Follow them. I'll take care of this.

27
00:01:58,160 --> 00:01:59,160
Go!

28
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:10,360
Argh!

29
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:06,000
"When Light Fades" (Episode 5)

30
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:15,760
Why haven't they returned yet?

31
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:17,880
They're back.

32
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:19,280
Our comrades-in-arms are back.

33
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:22,640
Let's take care of the
wounded comrades. Quick!

34
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Comrade Yue.

35
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:35,400
Bai Tong.

36
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,000
Bai Tong, calm down.

37
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:38,639
Where's my dad?

38
00:04:38,640 --> 00:04:39,640
Calm down.

39
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:42,159
Where's my dad?

40
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:43,720
Bai Tong, calm down.

41
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:45,400
Where's Comrade Ploeng?

42
00:04:48,400 --> 00:04:50,079
Dad... Dad!

43
00:04:50,080 --> 00:04:51,760
Bai Tong, please no.

44
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:54,880
Where's Comrade Ploeng?

45
00:04:55,320 --> 00:04:56,800
I'll take you there.

46
00:04:58,240 --> 00:05:00,600
- Let me go.
- Bai Tong.

47
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:04,440
I'll rescue my dad.

48
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:06,640
I'll go too.

49
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,280
Stay here. Don't mess around.

50
00:05:09,760 --> 00:05:11,919
It's OK, Bai Tong. Relax.

51
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:13,280
Listen to me, Bai Tong.

52
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:28,800
Comrade Ploeng, Comrade Ploeng...

53
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:30,840
Comrade Ploeng.

54
00:05:32,640 --> 00:05:33,800
Comrade Ploeng.

55
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:43,920
Dad!

56
00:05:43,921 --> 00:05:46,040
Bai Tong.

57
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:49,159
Bai Tong, calm down.

58
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:50,160
Dad!

59
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:52,200
Dad!

60
00:05:53,480 --> 00:05:55,199
I want to see my dad.

61
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:56,639
Bai Tong.

62
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:57,839
Bai Tong, calm down.

63
00:05:57,840 --> 00:06:02,040
No, I want to see my dad.

64
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:05,719
Bai Tong, please calm down.

65
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:08,080
It's OK, Bai Tong.

66
00:06:10,320 --> 00:06:11,519
Bai Tong, calm down.

67
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:14,320
No, no!

68
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:17,080
Bai Tong, listen to me.

69
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:20,920
I want to see my dad.

70
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:23,400
Bai Tong, please calm down.

71
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:57,800
You told me you would
take me out of the forest.

72
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:02,720
Why did you leave me alone like this?

73
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:06,240
Am I beautiful, dad?

74
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:07,600
Oh!

75
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:08,480
Ha ha.

76
00:07:08,960 --> 00:07:10,120
Yes, you really are.

77
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:12,520
You know...

78
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:16,320
I and all comrades are tasked
with protecting the base.

79
00:07:17,320 --> 00:07:19,280
To make everyone in
the base safe and sound.

80
00:07:19,840 --> 00:07:21,360
If we win the battle,

81
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:25,120
we won't have to hold guns any longer.

82
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:29,000
Dad, let's win the battle,
and take me out of here.

83
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:31,480
Ha ha.

84
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:33,920
Yes maam, my girl.

85
00:08:23,520 --> 00:08:26,000
We don't need to win.

86
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:30,440
Just bring my dad back—that's enough.

87
00:09:19,840 --> 00:09:21,480
You once said,

88
00:09:22,640 --> 00:09:23,680
you don't like the battle-

89
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:26,240
-because it's brutal.

90
00:09:29,480 --> 00:09:31,000
But what's even more brutal-

91
00:09:32,520 --> 00:09:34,280
-is what comes after.

92
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:39,480
Every time we finnish the battle,

93
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:43,520
Comrade Ploeng...

94
00:09:45,640 --> 00:09:47,640
Comrade Ploeng would
take me to the battlefield...

95
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:51,400
to bring all the bodies back to the base.

96
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:01,440
Comrade Ploeng taught me...

97
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:05,600
we need to bring everyone...

98
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:08,080
to go back to the base no matter what.

99
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:15,280
It was supposed to be me.

100
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:19,640
I was supposed to go
instead of Comrade Ploeng.

101
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:25,480
So Comrade Bai Tong
wouldn't be left alone like this.

102
00:10:30,640 --> 00:10:32,120
What about me?

103
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:36,160
How can I live if you died?

104
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:51,120
With me,

105
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:54,200
you can feel free to cry.

106
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:10,560
It was supposed to be me.

107
00:11:18,440 --> 00:11:19,880
It was supposed to be me.

108
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:41,880
I'm sorry, Comrade Ploeng.

109
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:46,840
I didn't mean for this to happen.

110
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:56,880
I'm sorry.

111
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:05,200
You're so cruel.

112
00:12:05,680 --> 00:12:06,680
Do you know...

113
00:12:08,080 --> 00:12:09,119
Comrade Ploeng's daughter

114
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:11,080
lost her mom when she was born.

115
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:14,999
Now she's lost her dad.

116
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,600
How can she live?

117
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:20,840
I didn't want to do it.

118
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:23,760
It's a duty.

119
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:08,240
I'm sorry.

120
00:13:11,880 --> 00:13:12,880
Ouch!

121
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:18,240
There's a traitor in our base.

122
00:13:19,040 --> 00:13:20,239
Otherwise, there's no way-

123
00:13:20,240 --> 00:13:22,160
-they could've known
our battle plan in advance.

124
00:13:23,640 --> 00:13:24,960
Who do you suspect?

125
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:30,320
Any update on Yaguar, who I had you follow?

126
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:32,479
How can Yaguar be a traitor?

127
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:33,520
He's so naive.

128
00:13:34,760 --> 00:13:36,599
He's been acting strange recently.

129
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:37,960
Like he has a secret.

130
00:13:39,780 --> 00:13:41,260
People who look innocent like this...

131
00:13:42,040 --> 00:13:42,920
are the real danger.
Untrustworthy.

132
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:46,640
Especially the student comrades.

133
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:49,840
Why are we suspecting each other?

134
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:52,240
We can't trust anybody now.

135
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:55,840
If you find anything, report it at once.

136
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:08,440
Report Comrade Ploeng's
situation to the main base.

137
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:11,960
So they can appoint a new leader.

138
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:15,840
Comrade Ploeng died less than a day ago.

139
00:14:17,240 --> 00:14:18,800
You want to talk about
a new leader already?

140
00:14:20,880 --> 00:14:22,960
Sooner or later there
will be a new leader, right?

141
00:14:24,760 --> 00:14:26,120
Why drag it out?

142
00:14:49,960 --> 00:14:52,999
Comrade Bai Tong has
been crying since morning.

143
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,400
She has stayed all day,

144
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:09,600
Comrade Ploeng is never really gone.

145
00:15:10,800 --> 00:15:13,399
If you miss Comrade Ploeng,

146
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:15,960
he's always in your heart.

147
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:22,240
If Comrade Ploeng
saw you crying like this,

148
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,800
he'd be very worried, right?

149
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:33,360
Dad doesn't like me to cry.

150
00:15:34,760 --> 00:15:36,679
Being Comrade Ploeng's
daughter, I should not cry.

151
00:15:36,680 --> 00:15:37,840
Be strong.

152
00:15:38,680 --> 00:15:39,680
Very good.

153
00:15:44,240 --> 00:15:46,480
Let's go eat.

154
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:01,680
Since I heard the gunshots,

155
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:05,200
I realized how close death really is.

156
00:16:08,520 --> 00:16:10,480
Actually, I thought I had braced myself,

157
00:16:11,520 --> 00:16:13,640
But when the incident with
Comrade Ploeng happened,

158
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:18,240
I couldn't keep myself together.

159
00:16:23,120 --> 00:16:26,360
We never know when our turn will come.

160
00:16:28,040 --> 00:16:29,840
Don't jinx it.

161
00:16:36,240 --> 00:16:37,840
Life is short.

162
00:16:40,480 --> 00:16:42,640
We never know if tomorrow will come.

163
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:45,840
You and Comrade Ying

164
00:16:45,841 --> 00:16:47,321
seem to have something on your minds.

165
00:16:48,680 --> 00:16:49,840
You should talk it out,

166
00:16:50,960 --> 00:16:52,400
so you won't regret later.

167
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Let me help you.

168
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:05,800
Don't.

169
00:17:05,801 --> 00:17:06,920
Let's eat together.

170
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:09,640
I'll do the dishes too.

171
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:12,520
Why are you so strangely kind today?

172
00:17:13,120 --> 00:17:14,120
Mada.

173
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:22,200
Let's get back together.

174
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:29,720
I didn't mean to hurt you back then.

175
00:17:30,400 --> 00:17:32,200
I was really worried about you.

176
00:17:34,760 --> 00:17:36,000
I broke up with you,

177
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:39,720
because I didn't like who I was
when I was with you.

178
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:46,200
Having me as your lover,

179
00:17:47,720 --> 00:17:49,280
is it really that bad?

180
00:17:51,880 --> 00:17:53,720
You did nothing wrong, Sila.

181
00:17:55,840 --> 00:17:57,480
But we were too different.

182
00:17:58,600 --> 00:18:00,359
We can take it slow and adjust.

183
00:18:00,360 --> 00:18:02,119
Whatever you think or feel,

184
00:18:02,120 --> 00:18:04,280
I'll try to understand.

185
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:12,880
No need.

186
00:18:14,480 --> 00:18:16,039
I don't want to overthink.

187
00:18:16,040 --> 00:18:17,240
I don't want to be sad.

188
00:18:17,880 --> 00:18:19,920
I don't want to feel stupid again.

189
00:18:22,240 --> 00:18:23,840
If we go back to being friends,

190
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:26,920
maybe it'll be better than this.

191
00:18:39,480 --> 00:18:40,920
If we force it,

192
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:45,479
we'll hurt each other without meaning to.

193
00:18:45,480 --> 00:18:47,160
Then we will hate each other.

194
00:18:51,440 --> 00:18:53,120
I don't want to hate you.

195
00:18:56,120 --> 00:18:57,799
Let's break up while we're still in love.

196
00:18:57,800 --> 00:18:58,800
That's for the best.

197
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:12,640
So long, Comrade Gaun Hin.

198
00:19:45,480 --> 00:19:46,960
If you can turn back time,

199
00:19:48,760 --> 00:19:49,760
would you kill him?

200
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:53,400
I'd do the same.

201
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:58,280
I don't want you to die.

202
00:20:01,080 --> 00:20:02,400
Among the Hmong,

203
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:05,200
they give cockscomb flowers

204
00:20:05,640 --> 00:20:07,080
to someone they're interested in.

205
00:20:07,880 --> 00:20:09,320
It means...

206
00:20:11,040 --> 00:20:12,160
“I want to get to know you,”

207
00:20:13,200 --> 00:20:14,280
“I want to talk to you.”

208
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:26,080
I gave it to you. I'm not taking it back.

209
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:30,920
How can I live if you died?

210
00:20:40,520 --> 00:20:41,720
With me,

211
00:20:43,240 --> 00:20:44,640
you can feel free to cry.

212
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:54,360
Life is short.

213
00:20:56,960 --> 00:20:59,160
We never know if there's
a second chance tomorrow.

214
00:21:17,280 --> 00:21:18,719
I'm heading out of the base.

215
00:21:18,720 --> 00:21:20,159
Come with me, Comrade Saeng.

216
00:21:20,160 --> 00:21:21,439
Do we have a mission?

217
00:21:21,440 --> 00:21:22,440
No.

218
00:21:23,040 --> 00:21:24,160
Isn't it against the rules-

219
00:21:25,320 --> 00:21:26,520
-to go out without one?

220
00:21:29,880 --> 00:21:32,080
Where are we going, Comrade Yue?

221
00:21:33,080 --> 00:21:34,240
Somewhere.

222
00:21:36,480 --> 00:21:38,280
There are some scary
legends about the area.

223
00:21:39,960 --> 00:21:41,080
Ghosts?

224
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:47,880
Some people died there.

225
00:21:49,160 --> 00:21:51,320
People die everywhere.

226
00:21:52,600 --> 00:21:54,479
But if it becomes a legend,

227
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:57,200
it isn't just a normal death.

228
00:22:01,040 --> 00:22:02,360
Years ago,

229
00:22:03,360 --> 00:22:05,240
two male comrades were found to be in love.

230
00:22:06,960 --> 00:22:09,640
So they took their own
lives at Chan Siao Cave.

231
00:22:11,560 --> 00:22:13,640
It's not far from where we're going.

232
00:22:17,400 --> 00:22:18,560
Over there.

233
00:22:31,040 --> 00:22:32,040
Scared?

234
00:22:37,240 --> 00:22:38,640
I just feel sad.

235
00:22:39,520 --> 00:22:41,440
Comrade Yue, what
would you do if it were you?

236
00:22:48,120 --> 00:22:51,200
I'd do anything to be with my love,

237
00:22:53,360 --> 00:22:54,800
but in the end-

238
00:22:55,600 --> 00:22:56,960
-if I must choose between love-

239
00:22:58,080 --> 00:22:59,160
and his life...

240
00:23:02,840 --> 00:23:04,800
I'll do everything to keep him alive.

241
00:23:07,200 --> 00:23:08,560
Even I must sacrifice my own life.

242
00:23:23,600 --> 00:23:25,160
Comrade Yue, wait for me.

243
00:23:25,720 --> 00:23:27,560
Comrade Yue, wait for me.

244
00:23:31,280 --> 00:23:33,360
Watch your step, follow my footsteps.

245
00:23:38,680 --> 00:23:39,680
Are you OK?

246
00:23:57,680 --> 00:23:58,960
I'm thirsty.

247
00:24:02,800 --> 00:24:03,800
I'm really thirsty.

248
00:24:03,801 --> 00:24:04,840
Can I drink your water?

249
00:24:12,840 --> 00:24:14,120
Didn't you bring your own water?

250
00:24:17,520 --> 00:24:20,160
You rushed me, so I
didn't have time to grab it.

251
00:24:39,800 --> 00:24:42,040
So let's take a break here.

252
00:24:44,320 --> 00:24:46,080
Better?

253
00:25:09,440 --> 00:25:10,440
Wow!

254
00:25:11,040 --> 00:25:13,720
So this is what it's like. It's so beautiful
it makes people forget how tired they are.

255
00:25:14,440 --> 00:25:15,680
Woohoo!

256
00:25:23,160 --> 00:25:24,800
When I joined the troop in my first year,

257
00:25:26,160 --> 00:25:27,840
I was in a low mental state.

258
00:25:29,760 --> 00:25:31,640
It's Comrade Ploeng who brought me here.

259
00:25:33,560 --> 00:25:34,920
He told me to look down there.

260
00:25:37,520 --> 00:25:39,760
He taught me that when
your problems feel too big,

261
00:25:41,960 --> 00:25:43,440
if you step back a little,

262
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:46,640
they'll seem smaller.

263
00:25:50,360 --> 00:25:53,400
Back then I was living aimlessly.

264
00:25:55,320 --> 00:25:56,400
I volunteered for fighting.

265
00:26:00,200 --> 00:26:02,520
Because I don't have
any family members left.

266
00:26:06,120 --> 00:26:07,880
Comrade Ploeng told me...

267
00:26:09,040 --> 00:26:10,960
If you don't care about yourself,

268
00:26:12,800 --> 00:26:14,440
then find someone-

269
00:26:16,280 --> 00:26:18,000
-you want to take care of.

270
00:26:21,120 --> 00:26:22,440
Someone

271
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:27,800
you want to live your life for.

272
00:26:32,760 --> 00:26:34,240
If you find that person,

273
00:26:38,960 --> 00:26:40,080
bring them here.

274
00:26:43,960 --> 00:26:46,440
So you brought me here.

275
00:26:56,840 --> 00:26:59,000
I think you're my person.

276
00:27:11,720 --> 00:27:13,519
My name is Ravin.

277
00:27:13,520 --> 00:27:14,520
Ravin!

278
00:27:15,480 --> 00:27:17,440
The soldiers might hear us.

279
00:27:21,640 --> 00:27:23,000
You brought me a long way.

280
00:27:23,640 --> 00:27:24,680
This place is beautiful.

281
00:27:25,680 --> 00:27:27,519
Why don't you let yourself go a little?

282
00:27:27,520 --> 00:27:29,080
Try not to worry about anything.

283
00:27:31,760 --> 00:27:33,800
This is so damn fun!

284
00:27:40,160 --> 00:27:41,840
My name is Sasin.

285
00:27:44,040 --> 00:27:45,040
Sasin?

286
00:27:45,560 --> 00:27:46,680
Is Sasin your name?

287
00:27:48,200 --> 00:27:50,080
Aren't you afraid the
soldiers might hear it?

288
00:27:51,200 --> 00:27:52,560
I just brought you up here.

289
00:27:53,600 --> 00:27:55,120
There's nothing to be afraid of.

290
00:27:58,760 --> 00:28:01,600
I will protect Ravin with my life.

291
00:28:02,640 --> 00:28:05,000
So damn happy!

292
00:28:11,520 --> 00:28:13,800
When will the people
from the main base go out again?

293
00:28:15,920 --> 00:28:17,400
No one has been outside-

294
00:28:18,320 --> 00:28:19,960
-since Comrade Ploeng died.

295
00:28:20,320 --> 00:28:21,520
There's only Comrade Roong.

296
00:28:22,400 --> 00:28:23,920
She brought medicine to the villagers.

297
00:28:25,040 --> 00:28:26,120
Comrade Roong?

298
00:28:26,920 --> 00:28:28,040
Who's Comrade Roong?

299
00:28:28,800 --> 00:28:30,159
Comrade Roong is-

300
00:28:30,160 --> 00:28:32,760
-the female leader in Saeng Dao Base.

301
00:28:33,240 --> 00:28:35,360
She's the sister of Comrade Fah.

302
00:28:37,120 --> 00:28:38,320
Any news?

303
00:28:39,040 --> 00:28:40,239
Yaguar told me...

304
00:28:40,240 --> 00:28:42,440
they are investigating
the traitor in the base,

305
00:28:43,040 --> 00:28:45,640
and who shot Comrade Ploeng.

306
00:28:48,280 --> 00:28:49,280
Yang Sue.

307
00:28:50,480 --> 00:28:52,320
I have a task for you.

308
00:29:30,440 --> 00:29:32,080
What are you sitting here thinking about?

309
00:29:38,480 --> 00:29:39,880
I miss Comrade Ploeng.

310
00:29:47,040 --> 00:29:49,360
This compass, Comrade Ploeng gave it to me.

311
00:29:52,760 --> 00:29:54,240
He was like my father.

312
00:30:00,720 --> 00:30:02,000
I was named by him.

313
00:30:07,200 --> 00:30:09,040
Your name is Yue.

314
00:30:09,760 --> 00:30:11,359
I've wanted to know for a long time.

315
00:30:11,360 --> 00:30:13,640
What is the meaning of Yue?

316
00:30:21,160 --> 00:30:23,240
Yue is a Chinese word.

317
00:30:24,520 --> 00:30:25,879
It means the moon.

318
00:30:25,880 --> 00:30:26,880
It's written like this.

319
00:30:35,480 --> 00:30:37,600
And my name, Ravin.

320
00:30:38,600 --> 00:30:39,880
It means the sun.

321
00:30:41,240 --> 00:30:42,240
How do I write it?

322
00:30:42,760 --> 00:30:44,280
Can you write it?

323
00:30:45,560 --> 00:30:46,560
The sun.

324
00:30:48,960 --> 00:30:50,560
It can be written in Chinese like this.

325
00:30:56,520 --> 00:30:57,560
It pronounced as 'rì'

326
00:30:58,120 --> 00:30:59,520
Rì.

327
00:31:04,680 --> 00:31:06,440
Even though the sun and the moon...

328
00:31:08,280 --> 00:31:09,720
are both in the sky,

329
00:31:14,280 --> 00:31:15,680
they can't be next to each other.

330
00:31:18,480 --> 00:31:19,480
What if...

331
00:31:22,760 --> 00:31:23,760
I put the sun,

332
00:31:24,160 --> 00:31:25,160
'rì,

333
00:31:25,520 --> 00:31:26,720
right there.

334
00:31:27,200 --> 00:31:28,200
And put Yue-

335
00:31:30,080 --> 00:31:31,200
next to it like this.

336
00:31:33,520 --> 00:31:35,640
Does it mean anything?

337
00:31:41,960 --> 00:31:42,960
It does.

338
00:31:44,880 --> 00:31:47,120
If we place “rì” (the sun)
and “Yue” (the moon) together.

339
00:31:49,440 --> 00:31:51,439
The sun becomes smaller,

340
00:31:51,440 --> 00:31:55,040
as if it's being embraced by the moon.

341
00:31:57,120 --> 00:31:58,320
It read as 'Ming'.

342
00:31:58,800 --> 00:31:59,800
Ming?

343
00:32:00,240 --> 00:32:01,240
It means the light.

344
00:32:01,840 --> 00:32:02,840
The light.

345
00:32:04,760 --> 00:32:07,320
So the sun and the moon can be together.

346
00:32:08,080 --> 00:32:09,840
And they shine bright for each other.

347
00:32:29,240 --> 00:32:30,760
What's gotten into you?

348
00:32:31,840 --> 00:32:33,240
You were just smiling a second ago.

349
00:32:36,080 --> 00:32:37,760
Did I said something wrong?

350
00:32:42,400 --> 00:32:43,680
I killed a person,

351
00:32:44,760 --> 00:32:46,240
then fled into the forest.

352
00:32:49,480 --> 00:32:51,160
How can I be your light?

353
00:32:58,080 --> 00:32:59,720
But you didn't intend to do it.

354
00:33:03,400 --> 00:33:06,480
It's still killing.

355
00:33:23,600 --> 00:33:24,760
At first, I thought...

356
00:33:27,800 --> 00:33:29,280
I wanted to kill him.

357
00:33:32,360 --> 00:33:34,320
He's the reason my father died.

358
00:33:38,400 --> 00:33:39,720
But in the end,

359
00:33:43,720 --> 00:33:45,240
when he finally died

360
00:33:49,240 --> 00:33:50,320
it made me hate myself.

361
00:33:55,760 --> 00:33:57,120
I became

362
00:33:58,120 --> 00:33:59,400
another bad person,

363
00:34:00,600 --> 00:34:01,920
who killed someone else's father.

364
00:34:08,800 --> 00:34:10,360
Don't think that way.

365
00:34:10,880 --> 00:34:12,800
There's no need to blame yourself.

366
00:34:13,720 --> 00:34:15,000
Just don't do it again.

367
00:34:34,800 --> 00:34:36,280
I'm not good at comforting people,

368
00:34:37,480 --> 00:34:38,840
but I want to comfort you.

369
00:34:53,840 --> 00:34:55,160
Feel better?

370
00:35:01,280 --> 00:35:02,280
Not yet.

371
00:35:03,960 --> 00:35:04,960
Not yet?

372
00:35:06,120 --> 00:35:07,360
What do I have to do?

373
00:35:20,120 --> 00:35:21,600
Better.

374
00:35:23,040 --> 00:35:24,520
Better.

375
00:35:25,440 --> 00:35:26,440
Let's go wash up.

376
00:35:27,960 --> 00:35:28,960
Go.

377
00:35:58,920 --> 00:35:59,960
What are you doing?

378
00:36:01,000 --> 00:36:02,799
If you're wet at night in the forest,

379
00:36:02,800 --> 00:36:03,840
you could freeze to death.

380
00:36:05,480 --> 00:36:06,960
You told me to go wash up.

381
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:09,360
If I don't go, how do I clean myself?

382
00:36:11,280 --> 00:36:12,680
I'll wipe you down.

383
00:36:13,680 --> 00:36:15,360
It'll be cleaner than taking a shower.

384
00:37:20,160 --> 00:37:21,200
Hurt?

385
00:37:24,320 --> 00:37:25,320
Not anymore.

386
00:37:48,440 --> 00:37:49,920
What?

387
00:38:00,640 --> 00:38:02,200
Why is your heart pounding?

388
00:38:23,200 --> 00:38:24,800
That's enough wiping.

389
00:38:30,280 --> 00:38:31,400
How is that enough?

390
00:38:32,240 --> 00:38:34,120
You said it'll be cleaner
than taking a shower.

391
00:38:37,560 --> 00:38:38,760
This is only the upper part.

392
00:38:44,120 --> 00:38:45,600
The lower part is...

393
00:38:55,640 --> 00:38:56,680
Why are you taking it off?

394
00:39:14,040 --> 00:39:15,320
Wipe it for me, please.

395
00:39:40,560 --> 00:39:41,560
Are you OK?

396
00:39:46,400 --> 00:39:47,680
What if I'm not?

397
00:39:50,480 --> 00:39:51,720
What should I do?

398
00:40:19,080 --> 00:40:20,240
Do you feel cold?

399
00:40:24,760 --> 00:40:25,960
Getting better?

400
00:40:42,880 --> 00:40:43,880
Getting better?

401
00:40:50,040 --> 00:40:51,360
You'll get warm soon.

402
00:41:40,800 --> 00:41:42,400
You're naughty.

403
00:41:44,200 --> 00:41:47,600
What would you do if I
were naughty and stubborn?

404
00:41:51,880 --> 00:41:53,560
Stubborn kids get punished.

405
00:42:29,840 --> 00:42:30,840
Are you scared?

406
00:42:34,880 --> 00:42:36,280
Or do you want to stop?

407
00:42:45,600 --> 00:42:48,280
If you want to keep
going, you can't stop now.

408
00:44:25,200 --> 00:44:26,600
I'm yours.

409
00:44:28,360 --> 00:44:30,200
And I'm yours.

410
00:45:19,000 --> 00:45:20,040
Can I have your knife?

411
00:45:22,120 --> 00:45:24,320
We just got together.
You're already trying to kill me?

412
00:45:24,600 --> 00:45:25,600
Please.

413
00:46:09,520 --> 00:46:10,520
Come on.

414
00:46:13,600 --> 00:46:16,359
This tree will be our witness.

415
00:46:16,360 --> 00:46:18,919
No matter what happens,

416
00:46:18,920 --> 00:46:20,520
we will get through it together.

417
00:46:41,800 --> 00:46:43,319
Why are you giving me a gun?

418
00:46:43,320 --> 00:46:44,720
Do you want me to shoot now?

419
00:46:45,240 --> 00:46:46,280
Look closely.

420
00:46:50,640 --> 00:46:53,159
(Sasin Ngaochan.)

421
00:46:53,160 --> 00:46:55,480
So you'll feel like I'm
always here with you.

422
00:46:57,640 --> 00:47:00,080
I want you to always
be right by my side, too.

423
00:47:03,480 --> 00:47:05,040
Here's mine.

424
00:47:09,400 --> 00:47:12,160
Ravin Chaichan.

425
00:47:12,640 --> 00:47:15,000
Hey! Do you know my last name?

426
00:47:16,800 --> 00:47:18,640
Every student who fled to the forest,

427
00:47:19,360 --> 00:47:21,320
Where they studied, what their names are...

428
00:47:21,600 --> 00:47:22,680
I have all the information.

429
00:47:24,120 --> 00:47:26,320
But you… I've remembered
since the first day.

430
00:47:27,400 --> 00:47:28,599
You remember that well.

431
00:47:28,600 --> 00:47:31,040
Did you have a crush on
me the first time we met?

432
00:47:33,400 --> 00:47:34,999
When I first met you,

433
00:47:35,000 --> 00:47:36,639
I thought you were-

434
00:47:36,640 --> 00:47:38,080
-a mischievous kid.

435
00:47:45,560 --> 00:47:47,040
What about now?

436
00:47:48,840 --> 00:47:50,600
How do you feel?

437
00:47:53,880 --> 00:47:54,960
This is how I feel.

438
00:47:55,640 --> 00:47:57,360
What are you doing? I'm blushing.

439
00:47:59,360 --> 00:48:00,360
Do you like it?

440
00:48:21,600 --> 00:48:24,640
Time flies when we're happy.

441
00:48:25,440 --> 00:48:27,400
I won't be able to be
near you when we go back.

442
00:48:29,280 --> 00:48:30,400
Yes, you will, Vin.

443
00:48:35,080 --> 00:48:36,560
What did you call me?

444
00:48:37,480 --> 00:48:38,760
Your nickname is Vin, right?

445
00:48:39,800 --> 00:48:41,640
I heard Comrade Gaun
Hin called you with that.

446
00:48:41,960 --> 00:48:43,440
So you won't call me comrade?

447
00:48:45,920 --> 00:48:48,560
Well... we are more than comrades now.

448
00:48:49,320 --> 00:48:51,240
So do we have to call
each other something else?

449
00:48:52,000 --> 00:48:53,000
And...

450
00:48:53,920 --> 00:48:55,240
What are we now?

451
00:48:58,240 --> 00:48:59,560
Alright, I'll stop teasing you.

452
00:49:01,360 --> 00:49:03,200
What do you want me to call you?

453
00:49:06,440 --> 00:49:07,480
Sin is OK.

454
00:49:40,400 --> 00:49:41,760
Someone's here.

455
00:49:47,080 --> 00:49:48,840
A patrol comrade said...

456
00:49:49,480 --> 00:49:51,040
you left the base last night.

457
00:49:52,360 --> 00:49:53,440
Where did you go?

458
00:49:55,080 --> 00:49:56,080
We had some business.

459
00:49:56,520 --> 00:49:57,640
What kind of business?

460
00:49:58,320 --> 00:49:59,320
What's going on?

461
00:50:05,920 --> 00:50:07,640
Comrade Saeng, you go on ahead to the base.

462
00:50:08,200 --> 00:50:09,200
Yes sir.

463
00:50:17,840 --> 00:50:18,840
So?

464
00:50:20,240 --> 00:50:21,320
Yang Sue reported...

465
00:50:22,160 --> 00:50:24,680
there's a rumor about Captain Dan Din
among the villagers.

466
00:50:25,880 --> 00:50:26,880
Dan Din?

467
00:50:27,280 --> 00:50:28,240
Word is, Dan Din's

468
00:50:28,241 --> 00:50:31,079
been moving between
the base and the village,

469
00:50:31,080 --> 00:50:32,840
where the villagers gather.

470
00:50:33,680 --> 00:50:35,360
He's expected to come back again tomorrow.

471
00:50:35,977 --> 00:50:37,296
How is the main base reacting?

472
00:50:37,320 --> 00:50:39,439
We've reported it since the
day Comrade Ploeng died.

473
00:50:39,440 --> 00:50:41,200
But they've never sent
any orders down here.

474
00:50:43,360 --> 00:50:44,360
Good.

475
00:50:45,040 --> 00:50:46,040
If he comes again,

476
00:50:46,640 --> 00:50:47,880
I'll kill him.

477
00:50:51,680 --> 00:50:52,879
If we kill the son of
a high-ranking soldier

478
00:50:52,880 --> 00:50:54,040
outside the battlefield,

479
00:50:55,520 --> 00:50:57,760
that would mean we're going
to war with the authorities.

480
00:50:59,160 --> 00:51:00,479
One more thing,

481
00:51:00,480 --> 00:51:02,119
There's no orders from the main base.

482
00:51:02,120 --> 00:51:03,960
So we shouldn't act on our own.

483
00:51:05,800 --> 00:51:07,080
The most important thing is...

484
00:51:08,120 --> 00:51:10,000
to avenge Comrade Ploeng.

485
00:51:11,360 --> 00:51:12,600
Whoever is a coward, stay here.

486
00:51:13,600 --> 00:51:15,000
But I'll go.

487
00:51:18,680 --> 00:51:19,680
I'll go with you.

488
00:51:49,080 --> 00:51:50,080
Comrade Yue.

489
00:51:50,081 --> 00:51:51,240
Comrade Yue, are you there?

490
00:51:52,120 --> 00:51:53,120
Yes, I am.

491
00:52:01,640 --> 00:52:03,360
I brought you some food.

492
00:52:09,560 --> 00:52:11,759
What are you doing? Working?

493
00:52:11,760 --> 00:52:12,760
Nope.

494
00:52:13,240 --> 00:52:14,480
I'd better not bother you.

495
00:52:21,040 --> 00:52:23,320
I'll go on the mission with
Comrade Fah tomorrow.

496
00:52:26,560 --> 00:52:27,560
You stay here. Be good.

497
00:52:30,400 --> 00:52:32,640
What's the mission? Fighting again?

498
00:52:33,120 --> 00:52:34,120
No, not fighting.

499
00:52:34,920 --> 00:52:36,119
Just going down to the village.

500
00:52:36,120 --> 00:52:37,120
I'll be back soon.

501
00:52:38,960 --> 00:52:39,960
Let's eat first.

502
00:52:40,000 --> 00:52:41,000
Muah.

503
00:52:42,480 --> 00:52:43,360
Let's eat.
Muah.

504
00:52:45,320 --> 00:52:46,480
No kissing, Eat.

505
00:52:48,320 --> 00:52:49,320
So sweet.

506
00:52:50,720 --> 00:52:51,839
What's this?

507
00:52:51,840 --> 00:52:52,840
This is what eating is.

508
00:52:53,840 --> 00:52:54,840
The food is here.

509
00:52:54,960 --> 00:52:55,960
The food is here.

510
00:52:56,880 --> 00:52:57,880
Here.

511
00:52:58,240 --> 00:52:59,959
Kisses won't fill you up, but food will.

512
00:52:59,960 --> 00:53:00,960
It won't.

513
00:53:02,360 --> 00:53:03,520
Still not full?

514
00:53:05,440 --> 00:53:06,320
Are you full yet?
I'm full.

515
00:53:08,400 --> 00:53:09,400
But I'm not.

516
00:53:11,960 --> 00:53:12,960
I'm not full yet.

517
00:53:17,160 --> 00:53:18,760
Eat your food. Stop kissing me.

518
00:53:57,440 --> 00:53:58,440
Hey!

519
00:54:06,680 --> 00:54:09,119
Get up! I said get up! Get up!

520
00:54:09,120 --> 00:54:10,120
Ouch!
